    "lawCode": "Amd §1236, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2250\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to reflector\nand lamp equipment on bicycles\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nWill allow bicycle operators the option of equipping their bicycles\nwith amber or red lights on the rear of bicycles.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nAll bicycles operated one-half hour prior to sunrise and/or one-half\nhour after sunset, shall be required to be equipped with either a red\nor amber light on the rear of the bicycle. Such light must be visible\nfrom a distance of at least 300 feet. Amends subdivision (a) of\nSection 1236 of the Vehicle and Traffic Law.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nPresent Law does not allow for an amber light on the rear of a\nbicycle.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nRecent studies have shown that amber lights provide the maximum amount\nof visibility. This legislation will allow bicyclists to equip their\nbicycles with either amber or red rear fender lights.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2007-2008: A.518 - Passed Assembly\n2005-2006: A.3632 - Passed Assembly\n2003-2004: A.326 - Referred to Transportation\n2001-2002: A.2293 - Referred to Transportation\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nEffective on the first of November next succeeding the date on which\nit shall have become a law.\n",
